                <pb facs="0231" n="165" sameAs="frus:frus1934v05/pg165"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.3731/908: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Cuba</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-08-15T19:00:00-04:00">August 15, 1934—7
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>143. Your 393 and 394, August 15. You are authorized to insert at beginning of
                    new Article VI the phrase “on and after July 1, 1935.”</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
